\date{2025-11-04T02:49:23Z}
\title{Extended natural numbers}
\taxon{Definition}

\import{swarm-macros}

\p{We write #{\Ninf = \N \cup \{\infty\}} to denote the natural numbers adjoined with a
special positive infinity value.}

\ul{
  \li{Addition on #{\Ninf} satisfies #{n + \infty = \infty + n = \infty} for all #{n \in \Ninf}, and is standard on #{\N}.}
  \li{#{a \leq b} if and only if there exists #{c \in \Ninf} such that #{a + c = b}.  In other words, #{\leq} is standard on #{\N}, and #{n \leq \infty} for all #{n}.}
  \li{Multiplication is standard on #{\N}, with #{0 \times \infty = \infty \times 0 = 0} and #{n \times \infty = \infty \times n = \infty} for #{n > 0}.}
}

\p{Under these definitions, #{(\Ninf, +, 0, \times, 1)} forms an ordered semiring.}